  "body": "Found while gating #339 slice 2 (whether the mesh law needs to convict).\n\n**What happens:** the box fixture laws (`stack_span::band_struck`, via `Move::segments3` at `GOUGE_TOL` 0.01) sweep an XY arc's **inscribed** chords using each band's bare radius. The true arc bulges outward past every chord by up to the chord's sagitta, so fixture steel inside that sliver is not seen.\n\n**Measured:** an R30 arc with an r3 flute has a sagitta of 0.008–0.010 mm. With a box face half a sagitta inside the tool's true reach (the tool really goes 0.004–0.005 mm into it), `bands_vs_fixtures` returns no hit. This affects every fixture box. #339's mesh law can't help, because it only reads moves the box flagged (though its own arc reading already pads by sagitta plus `ARC_PAD`).\n\n**Fix:** pad `band_struck`'s radius per arc piece by that piece's sagitta, as `mesh_steel::chords` already does. Check XZ/YZ arcs and the posed chord walk the same way. #413 (XY arcs drawn as inside chords in the field engine and envelope scan) is the same family.\n\n**Done means:** an arc reaching a fixture by less than its sagitta reports `FixtureHit`; straight-move verdicts are unchanged; existing fixture suites keep their verdicts.",
